What I changed:

Clear database errors: a new handler in apps/api/app/main.py, with the logic in apps/api/app/db/errors.py, returns one of two specific messages instead of the generic one:

Login rejected or database unreachable: tells you to check that PostgreSQL is running and that the askdb_app credentials in .env match the database.
Missing table or column: tells you to run python scripts/migrate.py app upgrade head, then restart the API.
The Admin Center shows this text directly under "This view could not be loaded".

Safer SQL script: database\app\10_auth_governance.sql now upgrades an old llm_usage table in place. It renames the old columns, adds the missing ones, and points the foreign key at auth_users. It's safe to run more than once.

Tests: added tests/test_db_errors.py. It and the governance tests all pass (13 tests).

To fix it on your machine:

Make the database password match .env. Open SQL Shell (psql) as the postgres user and run ALTER ROLE askdb_app WITH PASSWORD '<the password in askdb\.env>';.
From the askdb folder, run python scripts/migrate.py app upgrade head. If you set up with the SQL scripts instead, re-run psql -U askdb_app -h localhost -d askdb_app -f database\app\10_auth_governance.sql.
Restart the API and open Admin Center. If a tab still fails, it will now say why. Send me that message and I'll fix it.
